      "side": 1,
      "message": "According to the openflow spec the difference between the cached generation id and new generation id should be:  \n\nI.e. distance() is the unsigned difference between the sequence numbers, interpreted as a two’s complement\nsigned value. This results in a positive distance if a is greater than b (in a circular sense) but\nless than “half the sequence number space” away from it. It results in a negative distance otherwise\n(a \u003c b).\n\nWhile the statement is confusing, it means that we should cater for a generation_id that wraps around and also allow for a difference up to half the difference between them.\n\nThoughts?",
